### Impact

Origin validation error leading to a confused-deputy abuse of the content API. An unauthenticated remote attacker needs only to get a signed-in TinaCMS editor to open one link — the payload lives in the URL fragment, so it never reaches the server or its logs. The attacker then reads anything the editor can read (including, on self-hosted setups, the `authentication` collection holding PBKDF2 password hashes) and performs any mutation the editor can perform (`updateDocument`, `createDocument`, `deleteDocument`), with results delivered to the attacker's own origin. Two boundaries are crossed: the browser same-origin policy, and the content API's authorization.

Impacted: every deployment serving the TinaCMS admin bundle (`tinacms build` output or `tinacms dev`). No configuration disables the `/~/*` route.

